{"title":"Kelvin","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Kelvin</b> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"SI\">SI</a> unit for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Temperature\" title=\"Temperature\">temperature</a>. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77c4aedd300b3792b3e610897de7095ddc769766.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\,\\mathrm{K}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" /> is defined as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Absolute_zero\" title=\"Absolute zero\">absolute zero</a>, the theoretical temperature at which there is no movement. It is defined by setting the Boltzmann constant to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d31229c975ca7167231ea5a7ac400f732364d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.380649 \\cdot 10^{-23} \\frac{\\text{J}}{\\text{K}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"38\" />, given the original definition of the meter, the kilogram, and the second.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conversion\">Conversion</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kelvin&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Conversion\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Kelvin to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Celsius\" title=\"Celsius\">Celsius</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a0a88e18c8fc21e5730219ab2441e67cc48113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^\\circ\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{K}+273.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" /></li>\n<li>Kelvin to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fahrenheit\" title=\"Fahrenheit\">Fahrenheit</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27ef47d36a36980152f2c3e555ce91b750de8a4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^\\circ\\mathrm{F}=\\tfrac{9}{5}\\cdot\\mathrm{K}-459.67$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" /></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Kelvin&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002712\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 28/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 830/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.406      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    7.406      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7392:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002712 and revision id 240111. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}